SteamARM: a fullscreen window keeps the whole head

Counter-Strike 2 in "Ventana a pantalla completa" (SDL, _NET_WM_STATE_FULLSCREEN)
ended up 1920x1058 on a 1920x1080 display: its own request for the display's
size went through validate_window_size, which keeps a title bar's height
free (1080 - 22). Its layer was then short of the display, the server did
not take it for a fullscreen game, and the Dock and the menu bar stayed over
it ("el dock siempre se ve por encima", the user). A fullscreen window's
ConfigureRequest now leaves it at its head's rectangle, and its size
validates to the head's size; the frame made again when it goes fullscreen
without its title bar is the head as well.
Leaving fullscreen validates the windowed frame it returns to (the
fullscreen size rule no longer applies to it); the head is the one of the
position the client asked for (a game moved to another display goes
fullscreen there); and the client is made to fill a head-sized frame
wherever the frame already had that size (a request for the head's size,
a frame made again, a window fullscreen before it was mapped).
